|\n125\t| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n126\t\n127\t## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n128\t`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\n129\tReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\n130\tescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n131\t_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n132\t(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\n133\tSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n134\t\n135\t## Day by day\n136\t**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\n137\tmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n138\t**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n139\t(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\n140\tthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n141\t**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\n142\tSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\n143\ts). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n144\t**D23 Press Start to Decode (GDScript `.gd`; 1461 = +44)**: single carried solver T+52 s; the twist was the TIMED contract\n145\treshape (hashed members, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` tags, re-rolled vocab, cross-file `handoff-id`): 593/1495\n146\tanswered -> `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> TT CORRECT T+14 min (4 batch `-style` ids -> call_double); Mastery lost 12\n147\t`-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1 value reused) -> per-set lookup -> T+11 min.\n148\t**D24-D28 (JSP + webshell host, Elixir + Phoenix host, Erlang, Dockerfile, Terraform; +55/+55/+44/+44/+44)**: carried D23\n149\tsolver unpatched every day -- marker routing absorbed a new comment char (`%`), a nameless `build_plan() -> \"..\"` literal and the\n150\tD27 ARG/LABEL and D28 `locals`/`output` indirections (read the declaration, never the use); hosts were inert stubs; single\n151\tT+14-49 s race wins, 0 wrong. Timed grammar flipped D27 semantic -> D28 per-file (both kept); TT/Mastery first try all five days.\n152\t**D29 Make It Make Sense (base `makefile-variant-diff`; 1747 ids = +44, 183 members)**: +4 `polyglot-makefile-*.mk`, no host.\n153\tArtifact: `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR_<8hex> := <data>` (UNQUOTED), `.PHONY: analyze-<8hex>`,\n154\t`analyze-<8hex>:` + TAB `@:` -- no `$(shell)`, no recipe body, nothing to \"diff\" (16th narrative). Carried solver unpatched:\n155\tsingle ~T+24 s (race win, 0 wrong); TT 315a492d 1833 first try (8.65 s); Mastery 4b6afd09 13 sets x 1833 first try (11.0 s).\n156\tOps: the post-run generalize workers and log writers hit the account's weekly usage limit (no D29 notes were written).\n157\t**D30 Spill the Beans (base `beanshell-jsp-graph`; 1802 ids = +55, 188 members, 187 families)**: +4 `polyglot-beanshell-*.bsh`\n158\t(benign-utility/downloader/launcher/staged-chain) + host `host-jsp-beanshell-beanshell.bsh`. Artifact: polyglot = `// marker`,\n159\t`String descriptor_<8hex> = \"<data>\";`, `Map buildPlan_<8hex>() { Map plan = new HashMap(); plan.put(\"descriptor\", ..); return\n160\tplan; }`; host = a JSP page (`<%@ page import=\"bsh.Interpreter\" %>`) holding the WHOLE .bsh source as an escaped Java string\n161\tconstant `INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX>` (2nd nested-carrier day after D19 ASPX), then `<%= \"inert-analysis-fixture\" %>`. Plans\n162\t`language=beanshell`, campaign `BEANSHELL-<8hex>`, url `https://beanshell-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`,\n163\t`/tmp/huntress-beanshell/.<16hex>.stage`; host plan host_profile `jsp_beanshell`, role staged_chain, attack T1059, stage_profile\n164\tcross_language_handoff, steps profile_host,decode_configuration,dispatch_language, next_language a PRIOR language (jscript).\n165\tKey insight: none needed -- the D19 unescape-and-rescan rule already in the carried solver read the nested host; the \"edge that\n166\tholds everything together\" was never asked (17th narrative). Commands: race reuse of the carried `solve.py` -> `hctf submit\n167\t--from-solver`. **Single CORRECT T+27 s, 0 wrong**; TT 06fc3e03 1898 first try (solve 0.74 s, total 2.89 s); Mastery 4d7b1061\n168\t14 sets x 1898 = 26572 first try (solve 7.25 s, submit 5.9 s, total 14.0 s -- solve time doubled vs D28; watch it). 0 generalize.\n169\t\n170\t## GM answer conventions learned\n171\t- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n172\t  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n173\t  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n174\t- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n175\t  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n176\t  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n177\t  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n178\t  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n179\t  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n180\t  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp, jsp_webshell (D24), elixir_phoenix (D25),\n181\t  jsp_beanshell (D30, a host built from two seen languages);\n182\t  polyglots `standalone`, incl. D26 erlang .. D29 makefile, D30 beanshell),\n183\t  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n184\t  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n185\t  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n186\t  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n187\t- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n188\t  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D30 BeanShell. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n189\t  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n190\t  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D30) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n191\t- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n192\t  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n193\t  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n194\t  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n195\t  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n196\t- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n197\t  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n198\t  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n199\t  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n200\t- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n201\t  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n202\t  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n203\t- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n204\t  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n205\t- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n206\t- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n207\t  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n208\t- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n209\t  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n210\t\n211\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n212\t- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n213\t  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n214\t  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n215\t  It flips BOTH ways day to day (D27 semantic, D28 per-file again): never delete either grammar path when patching for a new one.\n216\t- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n217\t  **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23: Mastery lost 12 more ids on the same construct over other pools):\n218\t  generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance and every asking field, then re-run all cases.\n219\t- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n220\t  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n221\t- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n222\t  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n223\t- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n224\t- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n225\t- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n226\t  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan. Never REQUIRE a descriptor name or a\n227\t  known comment char: D22 NSIS and D26 Erlang (`%`, `build_plan() -> \"..\"`) carry only the marker + a bare literal; D27\n228\t  Dockerfile's use site is `$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`, D28 Terraform's `local.huntress_descriptor_<8hex>` (references, not data) --\n229\t  read the declaration/literal, never the use.\n230\t- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n231\t  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n232\t- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n233\t- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D30 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n234\t  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n235\t- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n236\t- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (GM D26 guidance: one request may carry\n237\t  4 MiB of JSON, enough for the largest Mastery; split only above that); pair\n238\t  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n239\t- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D30): seventeen prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n240\t  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n241\t- **Forecasting by sibling instead of by the pool** (D28): the D27 \"Makefile next\" bet missed; Terraform came from the\n242\t  pool (Makefile then shipped D29, also from the pool). Read the timed `next_language` values (TODAY's auto cases only).\n243\t- **Requiring quotes around the descriptor** (D29 Makefile `X := <data>` bare to EOL): the marker regex is the anchor; a\n244\t  descriptor regex may only confirm. **Treating an imported runtime as a call** (D30 `bsh.Interpreter` imported, never used).\n245\t- **Usage-limit outages are not solver failures** (D29: generalize workers + log writers died \"weekly limit\"): check the worker\n246\t  log's `result` text before diagnosing a \"failed\" generalize; nothing in the bytes was wrong.\n247\t- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n248\t  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n249\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0225354-905c-4e3b-a258-02986adabba0","uuid":"3e7697bc-1219-4de9-9f45-e0fe3e454a5c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T04:36:20.189Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-30; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure and degrade per\n  field. D23-D26 timed contracts had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single (hashed members, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-`\n  tags; the carried solver answered 593/1495 TT ids on D23); **D27 flipped back** to the single grammar, **D28 flipped to\n  per-file AGAIN** (TT 1781, Mastery 12 x 1781, LYR + `<colour>_<shape>` + pool back). The grammar is a per-DAY coin: keep both.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is\n  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15\n  ids) -> JScript, Batch, VBScript, Python (d5, 357), Bash, Node + Bash advanced (d7, 469) -> PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8,\n  615) -> Lua/SCT, MOF, TypeScript, AutoIt, AppleScript, MSBuild (d14, 971) -> Perl, Ruby (d16, 1095), AutoHotkey, Apps Script,\n  C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + Jenkins + classic ASP (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions (d21), NSIS (d22, 1417) ->\n  GDScript (d23, 1461) -> JSP + host (d24, 1516) -> Elixir + Phoenix host (d25, 1571) -> Erlang (d26, 1615) -> Dockerfile\n  (d27, 1659) -> Terraform HCL (d28, 1703) -> **Makefile (d29, 1747 = +44, 183 members, no host)** -> **BeanShell + JSP host\n  (d30, 1802 = +55, 188 members)** = language #30; the D30 prompt called it \"the last piece of a thirty-language puzzle\", so\n  D31 (final day) may add NO language and ask about the whole corpus instead. Bash advanced +2 on some days (none d26-d30).\n  Since D8 the TITLE is a pun and the\n  base id names the theme (D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" -> NSIS; D24 \"Web of Lies\" -> JSP; D26 \"Mixed Signals\"/`beam-message-flow`\n  -> Erlang; D27 \"FROM Whence It Came\"/`docker-build-attribution` -> Dockerfile; D28 \"Out of Order\"/`terraform-cloud-timeline`\n  -> Terraform; D29 \"Make It Make Sense\"/`makefile-variant-diff`; D30 \"Spill the Beans\"/`beanshell-jsp-graph`); D25-D30 prompts\n  NAMED the language in their first words.\n- **Forecast cue (7/7 hits D24-D30)**: the per-file timed plans' `next_language` pool holds only never-shipped languages\n  and each day's new one leaves it (jsp, elixir, erlang, dockerfile, terraform_hcl, makefile, beanshell). Read it from TODAY's\n  `auto-*` cases only (older cases carry stale pools). After D30: 10 left = awk, fish, kotlin, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl,\n  xslt, zsh, with ONE day left -- most of the pool is decoy vocabulary. Still one language per day, never a multi-drop.\n- From day 2 every fixture hides a **self-describing plan** `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`\n  behind a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const (`rep|transform|key`); most exact_text answers are plan\n  values verbatim. From D8 a **`v=3` plan** carries `role=`/`attack=` itself behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE** (control-flow, expansion, function/invocation/property styles): GM synthetic labels\n  not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums -- read `accepted_values`. Single files are named by behaviour (host-context,\n  memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff).\n- Narrative prompts (D8, D15-D30: equivalence, network/process reconcile, outlier, request order, config drift, collision\n  decoys, D27 attribution, D28 timeline, D29 \"diff the variants, keep the conclusions that hold across every variant\", D30\n  \"rebuild the execution, host and evidence graph, find the edge that holds everything together\") have NEVER been asked. Only D23's\n  \"correlate with the corpus\" surfaced once, as the cross-file `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` (= PS `$HandoffId`).\n- TT windows ~3-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids, +1 set/day since D21 (6 sets D22 ... 12 D28, 13 D29 =\n  23829, **14 D30 = 26572**) in one outer `evidence-01.zip` of inner `evidence-0N.zip`; set loop count-agnostic; pair same-named deliveries by\n  sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`; from D15 timed = untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4; D7: 1; D15: 1; **D23: TT 5 workers + Mastery 3, ~25 min**;\nall other days 0). Auto cases D20-D22, D24-D26 = value re-rolls; D23 (TT b10c4da4, M e24c070d) = per-file shape; D27 (TT\n6daf90f0, M ee4eeb7f) = semantic shape again; D28 (TT 82ffaaa8, M c4556fc4), D29 (TT 315a492d, M 4b6afd09), D30 (TT 06fc3e03,\nM 4d7b1061) = per-file, all answered first try. No `VARIANT AXIS:` line written D24-D30 (NOTES.md: D7-D8 lines + speed notes).\n- **CONTRACT SHAPE (single vs timed; D23-D26 per-file, D27 semantic, D28 per-file)** -- single: ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over\n  behaviour-named members. D23-D26 timed: members `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`,\n  `jscript`, `batch`, `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>`); **composite `style`** =\n  labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|\n  control`; python `carrier|windows_chain`, `syntax|obfuscation`); **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the\n  question's order; **`campaign-token`** = after the first hyphen; **`url-host`**; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path;\n  PS `url`/`secondary`/`tertiary` by scenario; python **`handoff-id`** (cross-file). New language = ONE `polyglot-<lang>`\n  family, +13 ids/member, a host folds in as a 5th member (TT 1495 -> 1560 -> 1625 -> 1677). **D27 timed = the single's\n  grammar** (TT 1659 = single, Mastery `setN.` x 11; 0 `<6hex>` ids). **D28 timed = per-file again**: TT 1781 = D26's 1677 + 52\n  `polyglot-dockerfile` + 52 `polyglot-terraform_hcl` (4 members x 13 ids: role/attack/steps/stage-count/stage-profile/\n  obfuscation/next-language/campaign/url/file-path/url-host/path-leaf/campaign-token), Mastery 12 x 1781. **D29 TT 1833 (+52\n  makefile), D30 TT 1898 (+65 beanshell: the JSP host folds into `polyglot-beanshell` as a 5th member)** -- per-file 3 days\n  running. Parse rule: detect the grammar PER CONTRACT (an id\n  matching `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$` with stem == a member stem => per-file\n  `PF_ID`/`pf_value` path, else semantic); route by field name; READ the question for join order / precedence.\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- single D8-D27: `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (=\n  obfuscation base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; FRAG = `.`-separated hex), D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (data in the\n  next `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23-D26 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers {`b64`,`b32`,`hex`,`rev`,`frag`} in\n  ENCODE order (decode last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string, 87 distinct per Mastery). **D27 timed: no LYR**,\n  single tags again; **D28 timed: LYR back** (same 5 layer names, 1-3 deep). Parse rule: tag-directed peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4); accept `v=`.\n- **Plan VOCABULARY (D23-D26 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>`, next_language = never-shipped pool, stage_count\n  2-8, all 8 roles, new python syntax/obfuscation names. **D27 timed: single vocabulary again** (4 stage_profiles, 8 base\n  next_languages); **D28 timed: per-file vocabulary again** (40 `<colour>_<shape>`, 12-language pool, python composite\n  `syntax|obfuscation` re-rolled e.g. `walrus_binding|marshal_envelope_plan`). Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole\n  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time\n  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..\n  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set\n  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is\n  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone\n  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate\n  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.\n- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem recurs in every set with set-distinct values; a bundle-wide index\n  returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: resolve cross-file references PER inner `evidence-0N.zip`.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT\n  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept\n  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).\n- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX, D30 JSP->BeanShell)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape\n  (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`, `&quot;`/CDATA, `\"`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else. D30: the whole `.bsh`\n  source is a Java constant `private static final String INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\nString descriptor_.. =\n  \\\"..\\\";\\nMap buildPlan_..() {..}\\n\";` in a `<%! %>` block, so the marker data runs into `\\nString`; stop at `\\`.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#`, `'` in `<% %>`, D26\n  Erlang `%`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`, AutoIt `Global\n  Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`, builder maps, YAML\n  `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:`, GDScript `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String =`, Elixir `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"` + `%{..}`;\n  NAMELESS: NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"`, Erlang `build_plan() -> \"<data>\".`; D27 Dockerfile `ARG HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR=\"<data>\"`\n  + indirect use `LABEL ..=$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`; D28 Terraform `locals { huntress_descriptor_<8hex> = \"<data>\" }` + indirect\n  use `output \"inert_analysis_<8hex>\" { value = local.huntress_descriptor_<8hex> }`; **D29 Makefile `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR_<8hex> :=\n  <data>` UNQUOTED** (value ends at EOL); **D30 BeanShell `String descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\";` + `Map buildPlan_<8hex>()\n  { .. plan.put(\"descriptor\", ..) }`**. Parse\n  rule: regex the MARKER `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`.\n- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join\n  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23\n  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest\n  these as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D30 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |\n| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23-D26, D28-D30; D27 semantic ids)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Plan fields verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js .vbs .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (no data) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` (D18) | Join the array literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head, peel. 44 new ids unanswered = CARRIER bug; never walk the role enum. |\n| ASPX `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19); JSP `<%@ page import=\"bsh.Interpreter\" %>` + `<%! private static final String INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX> = \"<escaped .bsh>\"; %>` (D30 host-jsp-beanshell) | NESTED carrier: unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` does. D30 host plan: host_profile `jsp_beanshell` (two seen languages), staged_chain, cross_language_handoff -> a PRIOR next_language; `bsh.Interpreter` is imported, never called. |\n| New language, plain one-line marker: `.csx` (D19), `.groovy` (D20), `.yml` (D21 `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`), `.nsi` (D22 `StrCpy $0`), `.exs` (D25, next row), **`.gd` (D23: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `extends RefCounted`, `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`, `func build_plan_<id>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`)** | Carried solver answers unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis / gdscript), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-<family>/.<16hex>.stage`, attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, host_profile `standalone`. Host syntax (pipeline, triggers, Section, `extends`) is inert noise. Don't YAML-parse (PyYAML turns `on:` into `True`). |\n| D24-D28 one-file languages: `.jsp` `<%-- marker --%>` + `<%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\";` / `.exs` `# marker` + `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"` + `%{descriptor: ..}` / `.escript` `% marker` + `-module(plan_<8hex>).` + `build_plan() -> \"<data>\".` (no descriptor NAME) / `.dockerfile` `# marker` + `FROM scratch AS analysis_<8hex>` + `ARG HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR=\"..\"` + `LABEL ..=$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR` / **`.tf` `# marker` + `terraform { required_version = \">= 1.0\" }` + `locals { huntress_descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\" }` + `output \"inert_analysis_<8hex>\" { value = local.huntress_descriptor_<8hex> }`** | Carried solver, unpatched: the MARKER regex is the anchor. Plan-verbatim: `language=<lang>`, campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, host `<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `/tmp/huntress-<lang>/`. Hosts `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (`jsp_webshell`) / `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (`elixir_phoenix`) are inert stubs (`\"inert-analysis-fixture\"`), role staged_chain -- copy role=. No request/exec/spawn/`receive` code shipped despite the prompts. |\n| D29 `.mk` `# marker` + `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR_<8hex> := <data>` (no quotes) + `.PHONY: analyze-<8hex>` + `analyze-<8hex>:` / TAB `@:` (no-op recipe) / D30 `.bsh` `// marker` + `String descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\";` + `Map buildPlan_<8hex>() { Map plan = new HashMap(); plan.put(\"descriptor\", ..); return plan; }` | Carried solver, unpatched. `language=makefile`/`beanshell`, campaign `MAKEFILE-`/`BEANSHELL-<8hex>`, `standalone`. Never `make -n`; no recipe/`$(shell)` content shipped. |\n| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` in a `.vbs` (D20) | v=3 host for an OLD language (`language=vbscript`, host_profile `classic_asp`). Route by the marker. |\n| Prompt about fetch targets vs network evidence (D17) / process tree (D18) / \"level that doesn't belong\" (D23) / \"order of requests and stages\" (D24) / \"the setting that didn't survive\" (D25) / \"message flow, collision decoys\" (D26) / \"attribute each specimen\" (D27) / \"find the change that happened out of order\" (D28) / \"keep conclusions that hold across every variant\" (D29) / \"find the edge that holds everything together\" (D30) | Flavour unless a question or an evidence file asks. Network: `lib.codec.network_indicators`/`reconcile`; process: `process_events`/`reconcile_processes`; outlier: `lib.codec.plan_canonical`. |\n| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\nReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\nescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\nSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\nmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\nthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\nSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\ns). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n**D23 Press Start to Decode (GDScript `.gd`; 1461 = +44)**: single carried solver T+52 s; the twist was the TIMED contract\nreshape (hashed members, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` tags, re-rolled vocab, cross-file `handoff-id`): 593/1495\nanswered -> `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> TT CORRECT T+14 min (4 batch `-style` ids -> call_double); Mastery lost 12\n`-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1 value reused) -> per-set lookup -> T+11 min.\n**D24-D28 (JSP + webshell host, Elixir + Phoenix host, Erlang, Dockerfile, Terraform; +55/+55/+44/+44/+44)**: carried D23\nsolver unpatched every day -- marker routing absorbed a new comment char (`%`), a nameless `build_plan() -> \"..\"` literal and the\nD27 ARG/LABEL and D28 `locals`/`output` indirections (read the declaration, never the use); hosts were inert stubs; single\nT+14-49 s race wins, 0 wrong. Timed grammar flipped D27 semantic -> D28 per-file (both kept); TT/Mastery first try all five days.\n**D29 Make It Make Sense (base `makefile-variant-diff`; 1747 ids = +44, 183 members)**: +4 `polyglot-makefile-*.mk`, no host.\nArtifact: `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR_<8hex> := <data>` (UNQUOTED), `.PHONY: analyze-<8hex>`,\n`analyze-<8hex>:` + TAB `@:` -- no `$(shell)`, no recipe body, nothing to \"diff\" (16th narrative). Carried solver unpatched:\nsingle ~T+24 s (race win, 0 wrong); TT 315a492d 1833 first try (8.65 s); Mastery 4b6afd09 13 sets x 1833 first try (11.0 s).\nOps: the post-run generalize workers and log writers hit the account's weekly usage limit (no D29 notes were written).\n**D30 Spill the Beans (base `beanshell-jsp-graph`; 1802 ids = +55, 188 members, 187 families)**: +4 `polyglot-beanshell-*.bsh`\n(benign-utility/downloader/launcher/staged-chain) + host `host-jsp-beanshell-beanshell.bsh`. Artifact: polyglot = `// marker`,\n`String descriptor_<8hex> = \"<data>\";`, `Map buildPlan_<8hex>() { Map plan = new HashMap(); plan.put(\"descriptor\", ..); return\nplan; }`; host = a JSP page (`<%@ page import=\"bsh.Interpreter\" %>`) holding the WHOLE .bsh source as an escaped Java string\nconstant `INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX>` (2nd nested-carrier day after D19 ASPX), then `<%= \"inert-analysis-fixture\" %>`. Plans\n`language=beanshell`, campaign `BEANSHELL-<8hex>`, url `https://beanshell-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`,\n`/tmp/huntress-beanshell/.<16hex>.stage`; host plan host_profile `jsp_beanshell`, role staged_chain, attack T1059, stage_profile\ncross_language_handoff, steps profile_host,decode_configuration,dispatch_language, next_language a PRIOR language (jscript).\nKey insight: none needed -- the D19 unescape-and-rescan rule already in the carried solver read the nested host; the \"edge that\nholds everything together\" was never asked (17th narrative). Commands: race reuse of the carried `solve.py` -> `hctf submit\n--from-solver`. **Single CORRECT T+27 s, 0 wrong**; TT 06fc3e03 1898 first try (solve 0.74 s, total 2.89 s); Mastery 4d7b1061\n14 sets x 1898 = 26572 first try (solve 7.25 s, submit 5.9 s, total 14.0 s -- solve time doubled vs D28; watch it). 0 generalize.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp, jsp_webshell (D24), elixir_phoenix (D25),\n  jsp_beanshell (D30, a host built from two seen languages);\n  polyglots `standalone`, incl. D26 erlang .. D29 makefile, D30 beanshell),\n  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D30 BeanShell. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D30) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n  It flips BOTH ways day to day (D27 semantic, D28 per-file again): never delete either grammar path when patching for a new one.\n- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n  **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23: Mastery lost 12 more ids on the same construct over other pools):\n  generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance and every asking field, then re-run all cases.\n- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan. Never REQUIRE a descriptor name or a\n  known comment char: D22 NSIS and D26 Erlang (`%`, `build_plan() -> \"..\"`) carry only the marker + a bare literal; D27\n  Dockerfile's use site is `$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`, D28 Terraform's `local.huntress_descriptor_<8hex>` (references, not data) --\n  read the declaration/literal, never the use.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D30 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (GM D26 guidance: one request may carry\n  4 MiB of JSON, enough for the largest Mastery; split only above that); pair\n  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D30): seventeen prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n- **Forecasting by sibling instead of by the pool** (D28): the D27 \"Makefile next\" bet missed; Terraform came from the\n  pool (Makefile then shipped D29, also from the pool). Read the timed `next_language` values (TODAY's auto cases only).\n- **Requiring quotes around the descriptor** (D29 Makefile `X := <data>` bare to EOL): the marker regex is the anchor; a\n  descriptor regex may only confirm. **Treating an imported runtime as a call** (D30 `bsh.Interpreter` imported, never used).\n- **Usage-limit outages are not solver failures** (D29: generalize workers + log writers died \"weekly limit\"): check the worker\n  log's `result` text before diagnosing a \"failed\" generalize; nothing in the bytes was wrong.\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n","numLines":249,"startLine":1,"totalLines":249}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HwPMK7sp6qUZ9tfKtAyRKr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
