{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017B4HtcjCRXdHUJaaoQuEHZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D30 seen vs. D31 candidates)\n2\t\n3\tUpdated 2026-10-31 after D30 (D29's writer died on the weekly usage limit, so this covers D29 + D30). **D29** \"Make It Make\n4\tSense\" / `makefile-variant-diff`: single 1747 ids (+44, 183 members), 4 `polyglot-makefile-*.mk` -- `# marker`,\n5\t`HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR_<8hex> := <data>` (UNQUOTED), `.PHONY` + no-op `@:` recipe; no host. **D30** \"Spill the Beans\" /\n6\t`beanshell-jsp-graph`: single 1802 ids (+55, 188 members, 187 families), 4 `polyglot-beanshell-*.bsh` (`// marker`, `String\n7\tdescriptor_<8hex> = \"..\";`, `Map buildPlan_<8hex>()` + `plan.put`) + host `host-jsp-beanshell-beanshell.bsh` = a JSP page whose\n8\t`<%! %>` constant `INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX>` holds the whole escaped .bsh (2nd nested-carrier day after D19), host_profile\n9\t`jsp_beanshell`. Carried D23 solver answered both days UNPATCHED: single T+24 s / T+27 s (race wins, 0 wrong); timed per-file\n10\tagain both days (TT 1833 / 1898, Mastery 13 / 14 sets = 23829 / 26572) first try; D30 Mastery solve 7.25 s (doubled vs D28).\n11\t**Pool forecast 7/7** (makefile left after D29, beanshell after D30); 10 left (awk, fish, kotlin, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl,\n12\txslt, zsh) with ONE day left. The D30 prompt -- \"the last piece of a thirty-language puzzle ... rebuild the complete\n13\texecution, host, and evidence graph, and find the edge that holds everything together\" -- counts exactly 30 languages\n14\tshipped (PS .. BeanShell), so **D31 (finale) is likely a capstone: no new language, or one last pool language, plus the first\n15\treal corpus/graph question**. Narratives never asked: 17 in a row (D29 \"keep only the tradecraft conclusions that hold up\n16\tacross every variant\", D30 \"find the edge\"). Prebuild after D28 night built embedded-prior-script-dual-plan,\n17\tlyr-layer-vocab-extend, pool-language-host-wrappers, descriptor-decode-call-wrapper, make-recipe-inner-scripts (2nd try),\n18\tchange-order-anomaly, hcl-resource-dependency-timeline, multi-language-drop-battery -- the queue was empty.\n19\tRead with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\n20\tactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\n21\thave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n22\t\n23\tContext that drives the likelihood column:\n24\t- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n25\t  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n26\t  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n27\t  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n28\t  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n29\t  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n30\t  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n31\t  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n32\t  D18 solve.py and in lib.codec since D18 night). **D19 broke the raw-bytes assumption**: the ASPX host carries the whole\n33\t  inner script as an escaped string literal (`\\n`, `\\\"`), so marker data runs into `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is\n34\t  `\\\"`-quoted (lib.codec.v3_plan handles it; the carried solve.py needed a patch). D20 had no carrier twist. The real D21+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n35\t  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n36\t  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n37\t  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n38\t  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n39\t  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n40\t  -- yet (nor D19-D21's). D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n41\t  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n42\t  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\n43\t- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n44\t  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host),\n45\t  aspx_inline_csharp (D19: web-page host, file still named `.csx`), jenkins_pipeline + classic_asp (D20; classic_asp wraps\n46\t  VBScript = first host for a PRIOR language, first day with two host files); D21 GitHub Actions came as a LANGUAGE\n47\t  (`polyglot-github_actions`, profile standalone), not a host. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n48\t  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n49\t  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n50\t  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sidebar: