fun ..)`, `Pid ! {tag, V}`, `receive {tag, X} ->`, `register(name, Pid)`, `gen_server:call`, `handle_cast`; `send(pid, msg)`; `new Worker(`/`onmessage` | gap actor-message-flow-model (static send/receive edge list -> ordered flow) | low |\n| 102 | Specimen attribution / lineage (\"sharing strings doesn't mean sharing parents\"; build-stage, semantic and static-handoff evidence; \"skin-deep resemblance\") | gap (D27 prompt; no question shipped) | members sharing url hosts/campaign tokens/paths across languages; `FROM .. AS`/`COPY --from=` stage parents; plan `next_language`/next_stage/handoff_id edges | gap specimen-lineage-attribution (parent = static handoff edge, not string overlap) | low/med |\n\nCounts: 102 rows; seen 41 (rows 1-18, 22, 23 (BeanShell D30; Kotlin gap), 28 (Makefile D29), 29 (Dockerfile D27), 30 (GHA only),\n32 (Terraform D28), 35, 48-52, 67, 70, 75, 77 (JSP D24 + JSP->BeanShell host D30), 82 (NSIS D22), 89-91 + 94 (D23), 95 (Elixir D25,\nErlang D26)), gap 61 (row 102 opened by D27; rows 100-101 by D26; rows 96-99 by D24; rows 66, 68, 69, 71, 72, 78-81, 83-86, 88,\n92-93, 98-99 have lib support built; 87 given up). D29/D30 opened no new row (both were plain v=3 languages).\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS .scpt | MEI\\x0c/PYZ pyinstaller | 0d0d0a pyc | #@~^ Script-Encoder -> wshenc\nSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:  stages: -> GitLab  pool: -> Azure  kind: -> k8s  - hosts: -> ansible  $CHICAGO$ -> .inf\n #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n #Requires AutoHotkey / x := \"..\" / Map( / ; comments -> autohotkey v2 (D17; family polyglot-auto_hotkey, underscore)\n onOpen_ / DocumentApp / HtmlService / showSidebar / UrlFetchApp -> Google Apps Script (D18; polyglot-google_apps_script)\n ExcelScript./Office.onReady -> Office add-in  \"manifest_version\" -> browser ext  set x \"v\"/proc -> tcl  x <- v -> R  := -> go\n fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   final String x= / def f = { -> / pipeline{ -> groovy (D20)\n BEGIN{ / getline -> awk   HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR_x := <bare data> + .PHONY + TAB `@:` -> make (D29)   FROM/ARG/LABEL -> Dockerfile (D27)\n `//` marker + String descriptor_x = \"..\"; + Map buildPlan_x(){ plan.put(\"descriptor\",..) } -> beanshell (D30, .bsh)\n on:/jobs:/runs-on: + `# HUNTRESS..` line 1 + env HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR (no id) -> GH Actions (D21; polyglot-github_actions)\n Name/OutFile/Section + StrCpy $0 \"..\" + `;` marker -> NSIS (D22)  [Setup]/[Code] -> Inno  <Wix>/CustomAction -> WiX/MSI\n terraform{ + locals{ huntress_descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\" } + output{ value = local.x } -> terraform_hcl (D28)  Editor 5.00 -> .reg\n <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild   <%@ Page/runat=\"server\" -> ASPX (D19)   <%@ Language=VBScript %> -> classic ASP (D20)\n <%! String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24)  `#`+descriptor_x = +%{..} -> elixir (D25)  `%`+-module(+build_plan() -> \"..\". (no name) -> erlang (D26)\n extends RefCounted / const X: String = / func f() -> Dictionary: / `#` marker -> GDScript (D23)  [gd_scene/[gd_resource -> Godot\n resource (script/source = \"escaped\")  GDPC -> .pck  label start:/init python: -> Ren'Py  game:GetService -> Luau  @\"..\" -> Squirrel\n host-<profile>-<lang> may wrap an OLD language (D20 classic_asp VBScript) or pair two (D30 jsp_beanshell): marker first\n Sub AutoOpen/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA  =EXEC( -> XLM  __EventFilter -> MOF  #nullable/BuildPlan_ => -> csx (D19)  let/|> -> fsx\nPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n marker with NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n   `<TAG>-`, peel; other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})` `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`.\n marker data running into `\\n..` / `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX, D30 JSP INERT_BEANSHELL_x: inner script ESCAPED) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n D23 `LYR-<l1>_<l2>_<l3>-data` = ENCODE layers (b64 b32 hex rev frag): undo last-first; obfuscation answer = layer string\n copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code or a known list\nTIMED CONTRACT GRAMMAR: D23-D26 ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` over `<6hex>.<ext>` members -> route by field; composite fields =\n labels joined by `|` in the question's order; indicator = first present in the question's order; campaign-token = after 1st\n `-`; url-host/path-leaf from plan url/file_path; cross-file ids (handoff-id) resolved PER MASTERY SET. Diff id grammar first.\n Flips: D27 timed semantic; D28-D30 per-file (TT 1781/1833/1898, M 12/13/14 sets, LYR + pool; host folds in) -- keep BOTH.\nLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n XLM xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper | Python: exec->print under python3 -I, marshal->pycdc\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER run the fixture's interpreter (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File), Deparse/`make -n` (they execute), XSLT, plan URLs.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS: read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`, `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch expansion =\n STATEMENT table (D15+), but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (D23). A carried label rejected on unchanged\n bytes = regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh AND the asking field.\nNARRATIVE prompts D16-D30 (network/process/outlier/drift/flow/decoy/lineage/timeline/variant-diff/graph-edge): flavour 17/17\n unless asked; then lib.codec network_indicators+reconcile, handoff_graph, reconcile_processes, lineage, corpus_summary.\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..BeanShell).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D27 nights (see git history) and D28 night\nembedded-prior-script-dual-plan (`lib.codec.embedded_scripts`), lyr-layer-vocab-extend, pool-language-host-wrappers,\ndescriptor-decode-call-wrapper, make-recipe-inner-scripts (2nd try), change-order-anomaly (`order_anomalies`),\nhcl-resource-dependency-timeline, multi-language-drop-battery (whole-contract synthetic battery, both grammars). Corpus readers already in lib: handoff_graph/handoff_answer, corpus_links, lineage,\ncorpus_summary/corpus_answer. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router,\nfile-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route,\ncomposite-label-field-regime. Prebuild rules learned: only hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no `__import__`, no `tomllib`);\nkeep fixtures tiny (other lanes' slow fixtures under load have sunk script-lane attempts).\nPriority-1 order for D31 (finale; 30 languages declared complete on D30): the corpus GRAPH question the D30 prompt promised\n(bridge edge, host/execution/evidence edges, handoff target member), a capstone contract that adds only new suffixes on old\nfamilies, a 2-deep nested host, and the 15-set Mastery speed budget; then the D29\ncross-variant consensus, a marker/plan schema bump, a shipped graph evidence file, and a mixed-grammar contract.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"corpus-language-graph-bridge\", \"concept\": \"'find the edge that holds everything together' -- bridge/articulation edge of the corpus execution+host+evidence graph\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D30 prompt (base `beanshell-jsp-graph`): 'rebuild the complete execution, host, and evidence graph, and find the edge that holds everything together' -- never asked on D30, but D31 is the finale and 30 languages are now 'complete'. lib.codec.handoff_graph (built) already gives per-member next-stage edges; extend it: lib.codec.corpus_graph(plans_by_member, texts_by_member, set_scope) -> nodes = members AND languages; edges typed `execution` (plan next_language / next_stage / PS `$HandoffId`->python handoff_id), `host` (host_profile container -> inner language: classic_asp->vbscript, jsp_beanshell = jsp->beanshell, aspx_inline_csharp->csharp_script, jenkins_pipeline->groovy, wsf/hta/sct->jscript|vbscript, php_webshell, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, elixir_phoenix, jsp_webshell), `evidence` (shared campaign token / url host / file_path between members). Then graph_answer(g, question): bridges (Tarjan, edge whose removal disconnects), articulation points, max-betweenness edge, in/out degree, connected-component count, the language reached by most chains. Answer shapes to support: `src>dst` (ordered_tokens), member file name, language name, integer. Per Mastery set. Fixtures: a 6-member toy corpus with one bridge edge (host jsp->beanshell) and one cycle; assert bridge, articulation, counts. Stdlib only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"capstone-new-suffix-on-old-families\", \"concept\": \"finale contract with NO new language but new question suffixes on existing families (graph/host/consensus fields)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If D31 ships no 31st language (the D30 prompt closed a 'thirty-language puzzle'), the only new ids will be new FIELD suffixes on old families or one corpus-level family (e.g. `corpus-*`, `graph-*`, `capstone-*`, `<family>-host-language`, `-inner-language`, `-parent`, `-edge`, `-bridge`, `-degree`, `-component`). Prebuild a router in lib.codec: for an id the carried solver leaves unanswered, (1) plan_answer (longest plan-key suffix), (2) corpus_graph/graph_answer for graph words in the question (edge, bridge, connect, holds together, path, parent, child, reachable), (3) corpus_summary/corpus_answer for counts, (4) lineage for parent/attribution, (5) else NO answer (never guess into a bulk). Fixtures: a contract JSON with 6 such synthetic ids over a toy corpus; assert routing and that unknowns stay unanswered. Speed: whole-contract pass < 0.5 s.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"double-nested-host-carrier\", \"concept\": \"host inside host: a script escaped twice (e.g. WSF/HTA/JSP holding an ASPX/JSP that holds the script) -> unescape twice\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Nesting grew D19 (ASPX -> C# escaped once) and D30 (JSP -> BeanShell escaped once, `INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX> = \\\"// HUNTRESS..\\\\\\\\n..\\\\\\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\"`). A capstone could stack two seen hosts (jsp_webshell -> jsp_beanshell, classic_asp -> wsf_jscript, jenkins_pipeline -> groovy -> bsh): marker text then appears with DOUBLE escapes (`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `&amp;quot;`, CDATA inside an escaped string). Prebuild: make lib.codec.v3_plan unescape iteratively (up to 3 rounds of `\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\uXXXX`, `\\\"\\\"`, `&quot;`/`&amp;`, CDATA strip) until a marker peels to `v=`; return the INNERMOST plan for the file's ids and the host chain (outer->inner profiles) for graph questions. Fixtures: 2-deep JSP-in-JSP, VBS-in-WSF-in-HTA, with FRAG and HB64 tags; assert one plan, correct host chain.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-scale-bench-30k\", \"concept\": \"Mastery at 15 sets x ~1900-2000 ids (~28-30k) inside the timed budget\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Mastery grew +1 set/day: D28 12 x 1781 (solve 3.5 s), D29 13 x 1833 (5.7 s), D30 14 x 1898 = 26572 (solve 7.25 s, submit 5.9 s, total 14.0 s) -- solve time doubled in two days. D31 likely 15 sets (~28.5k, more if a language lands). Prebuild a synthetic bench (tiny fixtures replicated into a 15-set nested AES-free zip shape the solver accepts) that times the per-set analyse path and the answer-JSON serialisation, flags any per-member O(n^2) (e.g. per-member full-corpus scans in corpus/handoff lookups) and memoises per CONTENT sha256 within a process (never by id(obj): D25). Target: solve <= 5 s for 15 sets on an idle box. Report the top 5 hot functions; no network.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-member-resolve\", \"concept\": \"resolve a plan's next_language / next_stage to the concrete member it hands off to (same set)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D30 host plan: next_language = a PRIOR language (jscript) with stage_profile cross_language_handoff; D23 already asked one cross-file id (`python-<6hex>-handoff-id`). A graph question will need the TARGET member, not just the language: rank candidate members of that language in the same Mastery set by shared campaign token / url host / file_path stem / handoff id / role (staged_chain -> launcher|downloader), tie-break by file name. Prebuild lib.codec.resolve_handoff(member, plan, plans_by_member) -> (member_name, evidence) and wire it into handoff_graph; answers: member file name or `<6hex>.<ext>` stem in per-file mode. Fixtures: 2 jscript candidates, one sharing the campaign token; assert the right one.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cross-variant-consensus\", \"concept\": \"'keep only the conclusions that hold up across every variant' -- per-field consensus across Mastery sets / variants\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D29 prompt (base `makefile-variant-diff`): 'Diff them carefully, and keep only the tradecraft conclusions that hold up across every variant.' Never asked, but Mastery ships N sets of the same member stems with re-rolled values. Prebuild lib.codec.variant_consensus(plans_by_set) -> per (family, role) the fields whose value is identical in every set (role, attack, adapter, steps, host_profile, stage_profile typically stable; campaign/url/path re-roll) and the fields that differ; answer shapes: field name list joined by `|`/`,`, the invariant value, or the member that breaks consensus. Fixtures: 3 sets x 2 members with one deliberately divergent role.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-v2-marker-schema\", \"concept\": \"a finale schema bump: `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V2:` marker or `v=4` plan with new keys (edges, parent, host_language, inner)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The marker has been `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1` with plan `v=3` since D8; a capstone could bump it. Prebuild: accept `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\\\d+` (already) AND plans starting `v=4`/`v=5`, values containing `;`/`>`/`,` lists (`edges=a>b;b>c`, `parents=..`), nested `k:v` pairs, or a JSON object; plan_answer maps new keys generically (hyphen<->underscore, plural/singular), list values joined in the question's stated separator. Fixtures: V2 marker + v=4 plan with edges list in `#`, `//`, `<%-- --%>` hosts; assert all keys reachable and v=3 parsing unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graph-evidence-file-reconcile\", \"concept\": \"a shipped graph evidence file (edges JSON/CSV, DOT, GraphML, Mermaid) to reconcile against plan-derived edges\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17-D18 prompts named second evidence types that never shipped; D30 named an 'evidence graph'. If the finale ships one, it will be e.g. `graph.json` {nodes, edges:[{src,dst,kind}]}, `edges.csv`, `*.dot` (`a -> b [label=..]`), `*.graphml`, or Mermaid `A --> B`. Prebuild lib.codec.graph_evidence(path_or_text) -> normalised edge set (lowercased member/language names, kind) and reconcile_edges(declared=corpus_graph edges, observed) -> only-declared / only-observed / mismatched-kind edges. Fixtures: one of each format (tiny) with one one-sided edge; never render or execute anything.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mixed-grammar-single-contract\", \"concept\": \"one contract mixing the semantic (`<lang>-<role>-<field>`) and per-file (`<family>-<6hex>-<field>`) id grammars\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Timed grammar flipped D23 per-file -> D27 semantic -> D28-D30 per-file; the single stayed semantic. A finale could merge them (semantic ids for old members, `<6hex>` ids for new ones, or `setN.` prefixes on a single). Today the solver picks ONE grammar per contract. Prebuild a per-ID grammar router: classify each id independently (per-file iff the 6hex stem matches a member stem in the same set), answer each through its own path, and report the answered ratio per grammar. Fixtures: a contract with 50/50 mixed ids over 4 members; assert 100% answered and no cross-grammar collisions (`-campaign` vs `-campaign-token`).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try). D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try. D26 10 sets, D27 11 sets (semantic ids `setN.<lang>-<role>-<field>`); first try both days. D28: 12 sets, per-file ids again (`set1.polyglot-terraform_hcl-767e8f-..`), first try. D29 13 sets, D30 14 sets (per-file ids), first try both.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape. D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids). D26: unchanged a 4th time (TT 1677). **D27: REVERTED to the single's semantic grammar** (TT 1659 = single, Mastery 11 x 1659 = 18249, no 6hex stems, no LYR tags, no colour_shape stage_profile, next_language only base languages); the carried solver handled it because it keeps both grammars. Never delete the semantic path when a reshape lands; expect a further flip either way on D28-D31. **D28: flipped BACK to per-file** (TT 1781 = D26 1677 + 52 dockerfile + 52 terraform_hcl; Mastery 12 x 1781 = 21372; LYR tags, colour_shape stage_profile and the next_language pool all back); carried solver answered it unpatched. The grammar is chosen per day -- keep both paths and the answered-ratio check. D29 + D30: per-file again (TT 1833 = 1781 + 52 makefile; TT 1898 = 1833 + 65 beanshell incl. the folded JSP host), carried solver unpatched; still keep both paths for the finale.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"forecast the next language from the timed next_language pool (7/7 D24-D30)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Hits: jsp D24, elixir D25, erlang D26, dockerfile D27, terraform_hcl D28, makefile D29, beanshell D30 (each left the pool the day it shipped; D27 semantic timed hid the pool). After D30 10 left: awk, fish, kotlin, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh -- with one day left most are decoy vocabulary. Read only TODAY's auto-* expected.json `-next-language` values (older cases carry stale pools). On D31 first check whether the single grew at all (1802 + 44/55 = a language; +0 = capstone) before spending time on language forms.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-scale-final-days\", \"concept\": \"Mastery growth to 13-15 sets (+ multi-language days) vs the solve/submit budget\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D28 12 x 1781 solve 3.5 s / submit 6.2 s; D29 13 x 1833 solve 5.7 s / submit 4.6 s (11.0 s); D30 14 x 1898 = 26572 solve 7.25 s / submit 5.9 s (14.0 s). Solve time is now growing faster than the set count -- see prebuild gap mastery-scale-bench-30k. Keep one submit (GM: up to 4 MiB of JSON per request; split only above), fork per set, never re-index nested AES zips per set.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D30 (not needed D29/D30 -- the carried D19 unescape read the D30 JSP host): the solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs .escript .dockerfile .tf (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members). D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members). D26: `polyglot-erlang` (ERLANG-), no host. D27: `polyglot-dockerfile` (campaign DOCKERFILE-, url host dockerfile-.., /tmp/huntress-dockerfile/), no host; D28: `polyglot-terraform_hcl` (campaign TERRAFORM_HCL-, url host terraform_hcl-.., /tmp/huntress-terraform_hcl/), no host; per-file timed `polyglot-terraform_hcl-<6hex>-<field>`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":143,"startLine":162,"totalLines":304}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rx54EDMXrx1njLLYTPwoab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
